#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bheader.h1:3-4
msgid "¿Qué es la Peregrinación NSC?"
msgstr "What is the NSC Pilgrimage?"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.p:7-4
msgid ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Nuestra Señora de la Cristiandad – España </b>(NSC-E) es una "
"peregrinación anual al santuario de <a class=\"a5\" href=\"/"
"significacion\">Nuestra Señora de Covadonga (Asturias)</a> organizada por un "
"grupo de fieles católicos laicos devotos de la celebración de la Santa Misa "
"según la <b class=\"b8\">Forma Extraordinaria del Rito Romano</b>. Tiene "
"lugar en torno a la fiesta del <b class=\"b8\">Apóstol Santiago (25 de "
"julio)</b>, patrono de España."
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Our Lady of Christendom – Spain </b>(NSC-E) is an annual "
"pilgrimage to the shrine of <a class=\"a5\" href=\"/en/significacion\">Our "
"Lady of Covadonga (Asturias)</a> organised by a group of faithful lay "
"Catholics devoted to the celebration of the Holy Mass according to the <b "
"class=\"b8\">Extraordinary Form of the Roman Rite</b>. It takes place around "
"the feast of <b class=\"b8\">St. James the Apostle (July 25th)</b>, patron "
"saint of Spain."

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.h2:14-6
msgid "nuestro objetivo"
msgstr "our aim"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.p:15-6
msgid ""
"El objetivo de la peregrinación es la <b class=\"b8\">santificación del "
"alma</b> a través de las gracias pedidas a Nuestro Señor, por intercesión de "
"la Santísima Virgen María, ofreciéndole <b class=\"b8\">oraciones, "
"sacrificios y mortificaciones</b> durante tres días. En estos días de "
"peregrinación encomendamos especialmente a nuestra <b class=\"b8\">Patria y "
"al Santo Padre</b>."
msgstr ""
"The aim of the pilgrimage is the <b class=\"b8\">sanctification of the soul</"
"b> through the graces asked of Our Lord, through the intercession of the "
"Blessed Virgin Mary, by offering Him <b class=\"b8\">prayers, sacrifices and "
"mortifications</b> during three days. During these days of pilgrimage we "
"especially commend our <b class=\"b8\">Homeland and the Holy Father</b>."

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.p:20-5
msgid ""
"Buscamos contribuir a la restauración del espíritu de la Cristiandad —según "
"las posibilidades y siempre con el auxilio divino—, que ha dado a la Iglesia "
"y al mundo tantos santos, héroes y defensores de la Fe. Nos referimos al "
"orden social cristiano, el cual no es posible sino comprometiéndonos en la "
"restauración de todo en Cristo, comenzando por quienes peregrinamos, "
"nuestras familias, y los diversos ámbitos de la sociedad en que nos movemos."
msgstr ""
"We seek to contribute to the restoration of the spirit of Christendom —"
"according to our possibilities and always with divine help— which has given "
"the Church and the world so many saints, heroes and defenders of the Faith. "
"We refer to the Christian social order, which is only possible if we commit "
"ourselves to the restoration of all things in Christ, beginning with those "
"of us who go on pilgrimage, our families, and the various spheres of society "
"in which we move."

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.p:24-5
msgid ""
"Para tan osada empresa, depositamos nuestra confianza en el Santo Sacrificio "
"de la Misa, fundamento de la vida cristiana. Por ello, una parte importante "
"de nuestro apostolado es favorecer y estimular la devoción a la Santa Misa. "
"Durante la Peregrinación se busca resaltar y recordar los cuatro fines de la "
"Misa:"
msgstr ""
"For such a bold endeavour, we place our trust in the Holy Sacrifice of the "
"Mass, the foundation of Christian life. Therefore, an important part of our "
"apostolate is to foster and encourage devotion to the Holy Mass. During the "
"Pilgrimage we seek to highlight and recall the four ends of the Mass:"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.p:27-6
msgid ""
"La <b class=\"b8\">adoración</b>, para honrar a Dios de la forma más "
"conveniente"
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Adoration</b>, to honour God in the most fitting way"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.p:29-6
msgid ""
"La <b class=\"b8\">acción de gracias</b>, para agradecer a Dios por sus "
"inmensos dones"
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Thanksgiving</b>, to thank God for His immense gifts"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.p:31-6
msgid ""
"La <b class=\"b8\">propiciación</b>, por nuestros pecados y por las almas "
"del purgatorio"
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Propitiation</b>, for our sins and for the souls in purgatory"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div.p:33-6
msgid ""
"La <b class=\"b8\">súplica</b>, por nuestras necesidades particulares y por "
"las del mundo"
msgstr ""
"<b class=\"b8\">Supplication</b>, for our particular needs and those of the "
"world"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.p:35-5
msgid ""
"La Misa es el mismo Sacrificio de Cristo en la Cruz, ofrecido por el Hijo de "
"Dios al Padre Eterno, para obtener las gracias necesarias para la Salvación. "
"La Iglesia ha enseñado siempre que la Santa Liturgia es una de las vías por "
"las que el Buen Dios nos comunica su Gracia, o sea, la misma Vida "
"Trinitaria; nos enseña también las verdades de la Revelación de una manera "
"particularmente admirable (lex orandi, lex credendi), pues está inspirada en "
"palabras y actos de Nuestro Salvador. Teniendo esto en cuenta, NSC-E quiere "
"dar a conocer y amar la Misa celebrada según la <b class=\"b8\">Forma "
"Extraordinaria del Rito Romano</b>, cuya celebración fue favorecida y "
"recomendada por el motu proprio Summorum Pontificum del papa Benedicto XVI."
msgstr ""
"The Mass is the very Sacrifice of Christ on the Cross, offered by the Son of "
"God to the Eternal Father, to obtain the graces necessary for Salvation. The "
"Church has always taught that the Sacred Liturgy is one of the ways by which "
"the Good Lord communicates His Grace to us, that is, Trinitarian Life "
"itself; it also teaches us the truths of Revelation in a particularly "
"admirable way (lex orandi, lex credendi), for it is inspired by the words "
"and deeds of Our Saviour. With this in mind, NSC-E wishes to make known and "
"loved the Mass celebrated according to the <b class=\"b8\">Extraordinary "
"Form of the Roman Rite</b>, whose celebration was favoured and recommended "
"by Pope Benedict XVI’s motu proprio Summorum Pontificum."

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.p:36-5
msgid ""
"Queremos mostrar, entonces, la necesidad de restaurar el orden social "
"cristiano a través de las gracias recibidas en la Santa Misa. Por todo esto, "
"NSC-E realiza una peregrinación penitencial anual a Covadonga para pedirle a "
"nuestra Madre las gracias necesarias para poder llevar adelante esta tarea."
msgstr ""
"We wish to show, therefore, the need to restore the Christian social order "
"through the graces received in the Holy Mass. For all these reasons, NSC-E "
"makes an annual penitential pilgrimage to Covadonga to ask our Mother for "
"the graces needed to carry out this mission."

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.h2:40-5
msgid "¿Quién puede participar?"
msgstr "Who can participate?"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div:41-5
msgid ""
"Adultos <span class=\"span5\">Todo laico en buena forma física puede hacerlo "
"como peregrino caminante. Se peregrina en grupos denominados Capítulos.</"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"Adults <span class=\"span5\">Any layperson in good physical condition may "
"take part as a walking pilgrim. Pilgrims walk in groups called Chapters.</"
"span>"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div:45-5
msgid ""
"Familias y niños <span class=\"span5\">Pueden peregrinar niños desde los 6 "
"años. Las familias y los niños caminarán junto con los adultos en su "
"correspondiente capítulo, pero harán una ruta reducida, adaptada a sus "
"capacidades. El total cada día serán como máximo 14km.</span>"
msgstr ""
"Families and children <span class=\"span5\">Children aged 6 and over may "
"take part in the pilgrimage. Families and children walk alongside the "
"adults in their respective chapter, following a shorter route adapted to "
"their abilities, covering at most 14 km per day.</span>"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div:49-5
msgid ""
"Sacerdotes y religiosos <span class=\"span5\">Es indispensable su presencia "
"para proveer de ayuda espiritual a los peregrinos. No es necesario que "
"realicen la peregrinación completa, pueden participar incluso sólo un día o "
"durante ciertos tramos y ejercer su ministerio en los momentos de descanso. "
"NSC-E ofrece toda la asistencia necesaria para su movilidad y "
"avituallamiento.</span>"
msgstr ""
"Priests and religious <span class=\"span5\">Their presence is indispensable "
"to provide spiritual assistance to the pilgrims. They do not need to walk "
"the entire pilgrimage; they may participate even for a single day or along "
"certain stages and exercise their ministry during rest breaks. NSC-E "
"provides all necessary assistance for their transport and provisions.</span>"

#: pages/peregrinacion.html%2Bmain.section.div:53-5
msgid ""
"Voluntarios <span class=\"span5\">Aquellos laicos que no caminan, pero que "
"peregrinan de otro modo, ayudando voluntariamente en la logística y "
"organización de la Peregrinación.</span>"
msgstr ""
"Volunteers <span class=\"span5\">Laypeople who do not walk, yet make the "
"pilgrimage in another way by voluntarily assisting with the logistics and "
"organisation of the Pilgrimage.</span>"
